From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: End goes home and Call opens Phone

Owner decision 2026-11-19 (BBOS 10 and BBOS 7 profiles). The End (red) key
goes to the home page once setup is done and the keyguard is not up: Active
Frames on BBOS 10, the home screen on BBOS 7, because goHome() lands on the
SableOS home, which shows the page of the chosen profile. Holding End still
opens the power menu, and on the keyguard End keeps its screen-off behavior.
The Call (green) key opens Phone when no call is ringing or in progress; a
ringing call is still answered.
---
 .../com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
index 81c3887..d02d946 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
@@ -5570,8 +5570,12 @@
                     if (!mEndCallKeyHandled) {
                         mHandler.removeCallbacks(mEndCallLongPress);
                         if (!canceled) {
+                            // Sable: End goes to the home page (Active Frames on BBOS 10, the
+                            // home screen on BBOS 7) once setup is done; on the keyguard it keeps
+                            // the screen-off behavior.
                             if ((mEndcallBehavior
-                                    & Settings.System.END_BUTTON_BEHAVIOR_HOME) != 0) {
+                                    & Settings.System.END_BUTTON_BEHAVIOR_HOME) != 0
+                                    || (!keyguardOn() && isUserSetupComplete())) {
                                 if (goHome()) {
                                     break;
                                 }
@@ -5721,6 +5725,12 @@
                             // And *don't* pass this key thru to the current activity
                             // (which is presumably the InCallScreen.)
                             result &= ~ACTION_PASS_TO_USER;
+                        } else if (event.getRepeatCount() == 0 && !keyguardOn()
+                                && isUserSetupComplete() && !telecomManager.isInCall()) {
+                            // Sable: the Call key opens Phone (BBOS 10 and BBOS 7), as on the
+                            // BlackBerry. Never during a call, which keeps its own handling.
+                            startActivityAsUser(new Intent(Intent.ACTION_DIAL)
+                                    .addFlags(Intent.FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK), UserHandle.CURRENT);
                         }
                     }
                 }
